{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":1,"query":"name=King&limit=10&title=Gods of the Upper Air","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":[{"nonSort":{"@space":"preserve","#text":"The  "},"title":"reinvention of humanity ","subTitle":"a story of race, sex, gender and the discovery of culture "},{"@type":"uniform","@nameTitleGroup":"1","title":"Gods of the upper air"},{"@type":"alternative","title":"Gods of the upper air"}],"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":["King, Charles,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1967-"}],"role":[{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}},{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"author"}}],"nameIdentifier":"https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PBJyCy66M9WXtk3MFhpxMT3"},"typeOfResource":"text","genre":[{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"bibliography"},{"@authority":"marcgt","#text":"biography"},{"@authority":"rdacontent","#text":"text"},{"@authority":"aat","#text":"collective biographies."},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"fast","#text":"History"},{"@authority":"lcgft","#text":"Biographies."},{"@authority":"rvmgf","#text":"Biographies."}],"originInfo":[{"place":{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"enk"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"England"}]},"dateIssued":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2019"},"copyrightDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2019"},"issuance":"monographic"},{"@eventType":"publication","place":{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"London :"}},"agent":{"namePart":"The Bodley Head,","role":{"roleTerm":"publisher"}},"dateIssued":"2019."}],"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":[{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},{"@type":"media","@authority":"rdamedia","#text":"unmediated"},{"@type":"carrier","@authority":"rdacarrier","#text":"volume"}],"extent":"xii, 431 pages, 16 unnumbered pages of plates : illustrations ; 24 cm"},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"The Reinvention of Humanity tells the story of a small circle of renegade scientist-explorers who changed something profound: what it means to be normal. In the early twentieth century, these pioneering anthropologists, many of them women, made intrepid journeys that overturned our assumptions about race, sexuality, gender and the nature of human diversity, paving the way for the civil rights movements that followed and sparking a debate that continues to this day. From the Arctic to the South Pacific, from Haiti to Japan, they immersed themselves in distant or isolated communities, where they observed and documented radically different approaches to love and child-rearing, family structure and the relationship between women and men. With this evidence they were able to challenge the eras scientific consensus and deep-rooted Western belief that intelligence, ability and character are determined by a persons race or sex, and show that the roles people play in society are shaped in fact according to the immense variety of human cultures. Theirs were boundary-breaking lives, filled with scandal, romance, rivalry and tragedy. Those of Margaret Mead and her essential partner Ruth Benedict resulted in fame and notoriety. Those of Native American activist Ella Deloria and the African-American writer and ethnographer Zora Neale Hurston ended in poverty and obscurity; here their achievements are brought fully into the light for the first time. All were outsiders, including the controversial founder of their field, the wild-haired professor, German immigrant and revolutionary thinker, Franz Boas. The Reinvention of Humanity takes us on their globe-spanning adventures and shows how, together, these courageous and unconventional people created the moral universe we inhabit today.\"-- Book jacket"},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Away -- Baffin Island -- \"All is individuality\" -- Science and circuses -- Headhunters -- American empire -- \"A girl as frail as Margaret\" -- Coming of age -- Masses and mountaintops -- Indian country -- Living theory -- Spirit realms -- War and nonsense -- Home."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Charles King."},{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references and index."},"Also published with title: Gods of the upper air : how a circle of renegade anthropologists reinvented race, sex, and gender in the twentieth century."],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Anthropologists","genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Anthropology","Research","History"],"temporal":"20th century"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Anthropologists","geographic":"United States","genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Women anthropologists","genre":"Biography"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":["Anthropology","Research"]},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Anthropologues","genre":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Anthropologie","Recherche","Histoire"],"temporal":"20e siècle"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Anthropologues","geographic":"États-Unis","genre":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Femmes anthropologues","genre":"Biographies"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":["Anthropologie","Recherche"]},{"@authority":"eflch","topic":"Society"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Anthropologists"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":["Anthropology","Research"]},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Women anthropologists"},{"@authority":"ukslc","topic":"Society"},{"@authority":"fast","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Boas, Franz,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1858-1942"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePart":["Mead, Margaret,",{"@type":"date","#text":"1901-1978"}]}},{"@authority":"lcsh","name":{"@type":"personal","namePar